    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d178">

                <pb facs="0354" n="240" sameAs="frus:frus1924v01/pg240"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.2300/48: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Rumania</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dennis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bucharest</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-02-09T15:00:00+01:44"><hi rendition="#italic">February 9,
                                1924—3 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 9:10 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>7. My telegram no. 5, January 22, 10 a.m.<anchor n="16" xml:id="d178-f1"/> Note
                    received today from the Roumanian Government grants all permissions requested
                    but makes no mention of aerial photography.<anchor n="17" xml:id="d178-f2"/>
                    Foreign Office desires details of the expedition in due time.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dennis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d178-f1" n="16" xml:id="d178-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d178-f2" n="17" xml:id="d178-f2-content">
                <p>On June 14, 3 p.m., the Minister telegraphed that permission for aerial
                    photography was included in the note (file no. 811.2300/135).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
